        "original_id": "ef43840d-516d-5e62-9f99-86bf0d705d53",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gene Kelly, Liza Minnelli, George Abbott, Rosemary Lane\n- Works: Best Foot Forward, Flora the Red Menace, The Dangerous Christmas of Red Riding Hood, Cabaret, Liza with a \"Z\", Lucky Lady, A Matter of Time, New York, New York, The Act, The Rink, Stepping Out, Music from The Life: A New Musical, Sex and the City 2\n- Roles: director, choreographer, performer, dancer, actor, singer, film director, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Eugene Curran Kelly was born on August 23, 1912, and he became an American dancer, actor for film, stage, and television, singer, film director, producer, and choreographer.\n- Best Foot Forward was directed by George Abbott, choreographed by Gene Kelly, and starred Rosemary Lane.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to the original cast recording of Best Foot Forward in 1963.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to original cast recordings for Flora the Red Menace in 1965, The Act in 1977, The Rink in 1984, and Music from The Life: A New Musical in 1995.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to soundtrack albums for The Dangerous Christmas of Red Riding Hood in 1965, Cabaret and Liza with a \"Z\" in 1972, Lucky Lady in 1975, A Matter of Time in 1976, New York, New York in 1977, Stepping Out in 1991, and Sex and the City 2 in 2010.\n- Gene Kelly died on February 2, 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
